RESULT --> MANIFEST : final source inventory comparison

note bottom of INPUT_REQUEST
  The original request preserves its grant
  projection after the reported allowance
  has been consumed.
  Neither that retained approval nor the
  summary authorizes a replay or new build.
end note

note bottom of METADATA_RESULT
  The apparent byte sum counts each recorded
  file entry, so hard links can repeat
  the same underlying storage.
  Metadata alone cannot establish actual
  disk use or a usable compiler installation.
end note

note bottom of HOST_PACKET
  Compiler versions and a resolved library
  path identify candidate builder inputs,
  not successful native linking.
  The combined inspection stays bounded,
  while cleanup targets only this run's container.
end note

note bottom of INPUT_SOURCE
  Direct Fish selection bypasses the Mise
  shim that failed before syntax inspection.
  Passing mocked checks and parsing still
  does not establish packet availability
  or actual execution on the operator host.
end note

note bottom of HOST_RESULT
  The original summary preserves the fields
  that were unknown when it was recorded.
  New pasted facts can guide input selection
  without changing the old record or granting
  another inspection.
end note

note bottom of RUNTIME_REQUEST
  Keeping the same Rust userspace avoids
  a speculative GNU library transplant
  between unrelated runtime images.
  Copying only the pinned Bun interpreter
  still requires a real startup check.
end note

note bottom of HOST_DETAILS
  The pasted identity field differs from
  the retained registry configuration digest.
  That discrepancy has no established cause,
  so it cannot identify a wrong image
  or justify a new custody gate.
end note

note bottom of LIBDEVICE
  The archive digest cannot select a bitcode
  member or establish its extracted contents.
  Preparation records a separate member hash,
  because the downloaded archive and its bitcode
  contain different bytes.
end note

note bottom of APPROVAL
  Approval binds one run label so another
  label cannot replay the same approved work.
  Exclusive creation relies on retained evidence,
  not hardened custody across new containers.
end note

note bottom of ATTEMPT
  Recording the attempt before execution
  preserves evidence when stream capture fails.
  A retained exit code distinguishes failed
  capture after real work from a preflight
  failure that never started the command.
end note

note bottom of SOURCE_CHECK
  Post-check read failures mark bound sources
  as changed instead of discarding the result.
  The verifier retains failure data so a
  deleted input still produces a terminal
  receipt rather than an unrecorded exception.
end note

note bottom of LIMITS
  The total budget bounds only the test loop,
  so preflight and final receipt work remain
  outside that clock.
  A separate host invocation bound must cover
  those operations before execution is approved.
end note

note bottom of PACKET
  The consolidated packet keeps unresolved
  inputs and limits visible without approval.
  Its false operation flags distinguish
  proposed host work from fresh authority
  to perform that work.
end note

note bottom of FLAGS
  Flag output specifies compiler requirements,
  but no native build or relocation ran.
  The system library list cannot establish
  which other dependencies the runtime needs.
end note

note bottom of RECIPE
  Distinct build stages keep both production
  recipes unchanged for their existing roles.
  The runtime retains absolute target paths
  because compiled policy tests embed their
  subprocess locations.
end note

note bottom of ARTIFACTS
  Compiler artifacts supply test paths,
  while build script records cannot select tests.
  A successful Cargo exit and final build
  message are both necessary, because partial
  output does not establish a completed build.
end note

note bottom of RUNNER
  The cleanup reserve cannot fund another test,
  because campaign limits bound serial execution.
  The first rejected result stops the campaign
  without retry or automatic escalation.
end note

note bottom of COUNTS
  Frozen counts retain CPU coverage, even
  when a known harness contains no tests.
  A selected GPU fixture must pass once,
  because an empty selection proves nothing
  about execution of the numerical path.
end note

note bottom of MANIFEST
  The source manifest binds native inputs,
  runner code and unchanged supervision files.
  Checks before and after execution reject
  source changes, so a prior receipt cannot
  qualify a new build generation.
end note

note bottom of NUMERICS
  The full campaign keeps both coordinate
  sweeps and their existing error thresholds.
  Exact digests remain mandatory for the
  redundant learners, because tolerances could
  hide different updates after checkpoint reload.
end note

note bottom of RESULT
  Reported tests cannot enable training while
  canonical proof and normal job wiring remain
  unqualified on the selected host.
  The full functional path still needs separate
  acceptance, including reference and close facts.
end note

